--- body ---
## Context

Found by the 14-repo housekeeping sweep of 2026-11-09 (19:05-19:15 UTC, run
from the ~/CNRS session). `scripts/project-state.py --tests`, the probe yawn
and molt read, chooses a test command the project does not use and fails
silently under yawn's outer kill.

## Evidence

- Without a Makefile it runs bare `pytest --tb=no -q` (about lines 330-340).
  DOIfetch: exit 2, 24 collection errors
  `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'doifetch'`; the project's mandated
  `uv run pytest` passes 471 tests.
- arena: runs the full serial tier instead of the declared fast tier (11 s).
- The probe's internal TEST_TIMEOUT is 300 s, above yawn's 90 s outer kill.
  On arena and cadens (suite 253 s) the probe is killed before printing
  anything; yawn reports "tests unknown" or "housekeeping never".
- cired.digital: the probe reported main "synced" while local main had
  diverged 36/36 from origin after a history rewrite.

## Diagnosis

Established: the runner choice falls back to bare pytest whenever no Makefile
exists; the inner timeout is larger than the outer one; the sync check said
"synced" on a 36/36 divergence. Not established: whether the sync check
compares only ahead counts or only fast-forwardability (cause of the
divergence miss not isolated).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The probe prefers the project's declared runner: Makefile target first, then `uv run pytest` when `uv.lock` or `pyproject.toml` exists, bare pytest last
- [ ] A timeout is reported as such (inner timeout below the caller's outer kill, or output flushed before the kill)
- [ ] Divergence (ahead and behind both nonzero) is reported, not "synced"
- [ ] Tests cover the three cases

## Verify and Imagine (raid 4afdb3, 2026-11-09)
- Verified today: (a) bare `pytest` fallback at scripts/project-state.py:328-330; DOIfetch gives
  status fail "24 errors" (ModuleNotFoundError doifetch) while `uv run pytest --co` collects 472.
  (c) TEST_TIMEOUT=300 at :30; run() :38-44 maps TimeoutExpired to rc 1; the make branch reports
  detail "timeout", the pytest and npm branches an empty detail; JSON is printed only at :619, so
  an outer kill prints nothing. (d) the probe never says "synced": :59-64 defaults ahead,behind to
  0,0 and overwrites only when `rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...@{u}` succeeds; an
  unresolvable @{u} reads 0/0 silently; it compares HEAD with its upstream, not main with
  origin/main; yawn's prose rule never names the both-nonzero case.
- Premise corrections: arena has NO Makefile; its fast tier is prose in AGENTS.md (`uv run pytest
  -m "not integration and not slow"`), so criterion 1 as written still runs arena's full tier: a
  check-fast target is arena's to add (cross-project ticket). The 90 s outer kill exists nowhere in
  the harness (yawn SKILL.md:29 is a bare bash line): it came from the sweep's launcher or the
  runtime's Bash default; an inner constant "below 90" would track an absent stakeholder's value.
- Path: one `_pick_runner()` (Makefile targets matched with `^check-fast:|^check:|^test:` re.M, then
  `uv run [--frozen] pytest` when uv.lock or pyproject and `uv` on PATH, mirroring
  touched-tests.py:101 without importing it, then bare pytest, then npm); timeout as its own status
  with the caller passing the budget explicitly, or a partial JSON flushed before any kill, rather
  than a hard-coded OUTER_KILL; `diverged = ahead>0 and behind>0` plus `upstream: false` when
  rev-list fails; three tests with exact argv, TimeoutExpired → "timeout", "36\t36" → diverged and
  "36\t0" → not.
- Blind-Spot: below the severity floor on its face (no merge blocked, no state corrupted); the
  strongest case is the false "fail" on a green suite, which could send an agent to fix nothing.
- Author decisions: (1) keep as a ticket or fold the runner fix inline; (2) where the 90 s came
  from (ask the ~/CNRS sweep session) and whether the caller passes the timeout; (3) file arena
  and cadens check-fast tickets in their repos.
